<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/north-india-hill-stations/Leh-hill-station.jpg" title="Leh hill station" alt="Leh hill station, hill stations in india, north india hill stations, Leh" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Jammu & Kashmir<br />
<b>Area:</b> 1412sq.Kms<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 4500m above sea level.<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 25&#176;C to 27&#176;C , Winter 8&#176;C to 9&#176;C.<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b> June to late September</p>     
<p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Snow, mountains, River</p>

<p><b>Ladakh</b> is also known as the <b>Land of High Passes</b>, the Land of the Earth's Nomad Gompa, one of the most sought after destination when it comes to acting out of joy and adventure sports. Located in the northern part of India, Ladakh distance of about seven kilometers from the <b>Indus River</b> and its valley wide. India is full of places to the north, which are rich in natural beauty and places of adventure and fun.</p>

